      "sourceTextSha256": "6d02241e3aafe8f3b2d7707ee5c4e3eaa1bb21931bc82f22bc305ae3dfccbf4d",
      "text": "Breakfast. Full-day excursion to the Península Valdés Nature Reserve, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. After an hour’s drive, reach the picturesque village of Puerto Pirámides to embark on the traditional right-whale-watching trip. Lunch (not included) in Puerto Pirámides or Caleta Valdés. Cross the southern part of the peninsula, with its grasslands and gentle hills, past the Salina Grande and Salina Chica, around Punta Delgada at its southern tip, then on to Punta Cantor and the Atlantic coast, with the remarkable geological formation of Caleta Valdés, whose beaches are often home to southern elephant seals, the largest seals on the planet.\n\nOn the way back, stop at the Carlos Ameghino Interpretation Centre, a showcase of the peninsula’s natural wealth. Along the way, you have a good chance of seeing guanacos, lesser rheas (choiques), foxes, maras, armadillos and skunks. Return to the hotel.",
